    "ID-token test fixtures for src-tauri/src/ai/chatgpt.rs (public data only; no private key is kept).",
    "Each token is an RS256 JWT signed once with a throwaway 2048-bit key that was then deleted; jwk is its public half.",
    "Base claims: iss https://auth.openai.com, sub user-sub, aud [oaiapp_1], nonce N0NCE, iat NOW-10, exp NOW+3600,",
    "email writer@example.com, with NOW = 1800000000; each name says what differs (header kid k1 unless named kid_*).",
    "To regenerate: make a new key (openssl genpkey -algorithm RSA -pkeyopt rsa_keygen_bits:2048), sign each",
    "base64url(header).base64url(claims) with openssl dgst -sha256 -sign, replace jwk.n with the new modulus",
    "(openssl rsa -modulus, as base64url), and delete the key."
